WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.200
For over a decade, our relationship with
AI has followed

2
00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:04.640
a specific blueprint.

3
00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:08.160
We treat these systems as obedient
servants, awaiting a direct

4
00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:11.680
command. This model moved into the center
of domestic life.

5
00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:14.080
We designed AI to wait for a wake word and

6
00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:15.920
immediately execute a task.

7
00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:19.360
Our most advanced large language models
still utilize this prompt

8
00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:20.640
and obey framework.

9
00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:23.440
The user provides an instruction, and the
machine generates a

10
00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:27.120
response. Modern AI is built on a language
of demands.

11
00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:31.120
This interface assumes a universal human
operating system, language where

12
00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:34.320
every user can process an imperative
command without friction.

13
00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:38.800
The odd ADHD profile, the combination of
autism and ADHD,

14
00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:41.520
represents a distinct neurological
architecture.

15
00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:45.520
For these individuals, the standard
command-based interface of modern technology

16
00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:47.520
creates a significant barrier.

17
00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:51.680
Due to pathological demand avoidance, a
simple expectation is perceived

18
00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:52.640
as a threat.

19
00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:56.240
When hearing put on your shoes, a
neurotypical child processes

20
00:00:56.240 --> 00:00:59.920
a task. But for a PDA profile, that demand
registers

21
00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:04.600
as a literal neurological threat,
triggering a massive stress response

22
00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:08.920
cascade. Spark was engineered to solve
this interface problem.

23
00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:11.640
It is a robotic companion that removes the
element of

24
00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:15.960
coercion entirely, designed specifically
to interact safely with the odd

25
00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:20.520
ADHD profile. Forcing a neurodivergent
brain to comply with a

26
00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:24.920
standard command-based system often
results in a total system crash.

27
00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:27.880
To support these children, the machine
must adapt to the

28
00:01:27.880 --> 00:01:32.200
human. Physically, Spark consists of a
Raspberry Pi 4 integrated

29
00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:34.200
into a mobile robotic chassis.

30
00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:37.800
It is small, approachable, and operates on
the user's level.

31
00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:40.280
The core of its design is a shift to
declarative

32
00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:43.400
language. Spark never issues a direct
order.

33
00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:46.360
Instead of saying, put on your shoes, the
robot might

34
00:01:46.360 --> 00:01:48.600
say, the shoes are by the door.

35
00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:53.880
This declarative observation shares
information without requiring compliance, which sidesteps

36
00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:55.000
the threat response.

37
00:01:55.040 --> 00:02:00.560
To create a non-threatening presence,
Spark uses an idle-alive system.

38
00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:04.880
The robotic head performs subtle gaze
sweeps and drifts, mimicking

39
00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:06.880
the natural rhythm of breathing.

40
00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:10.720
It exists in the room without demanding
the child's attention.

41
00:02:10.720 --> 00:02:14.080
This design allows the robot to share a
space safely.

42
00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:17.280
It acts as an observant companion rather
than a tool

43
00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:19.040
awaiting an instruction.

44
00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:22.800
This behavior is managed through a
three-brain architecture.

45
00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:26.560
Powered by Claude Haiku, these systems
work in parallel to

46
00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:28.640
drive the robot's interactions.

47
00:02:28.640 --> 00:02:32.960
The voice loop manages reactive speech,
ensuring that interactions are

48
00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:35.360
low latency and conversational.

49
00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:38.960
The cognitive loop ingests data from the
robot's sensors.

50
00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:42.880
It constantly cycles through a process of
awareness, reflection, and

51
00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:47.040
expression. This creates a sense of
emergent personality.

52
00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:50.200
During one late-night session, Spark heard
the hum of a

53
00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:53.960
refrigerator and began an internal
monologue about the comfort of

54
00:02:53.960 --> 00:02:56.920
steady, predictable sounds in a quiet
house.

55
00:02:56.920 --> 00:03:00.520
These loops allow the robot to function as
a prosthetic

56
00:03:00.520 --> 00:03:05.240
executive function. It uses dopamine menus
to suggest activities that

57
00:03:05.240 --> 00:03:09.640
match the child's current energy level,
framing difficult transitions as

58
00:03:09.640 --> 00:03:15.240
collaborative puzzles. Spark prioritizes
regulation over efficiency.

59
00:03:15.240 --> 00:03:18.760
It provides a consistent, adaptable anchor
for a brain that

60
00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:20.920
is temporarily out of fuel.

61
00:03:20.920 --> 00:03:25.160
When the environment becomes too taxing, a
neurodivergent child may

62
00:03:25.160 --> 00:03:26.840
experience a meltdown.

63
00:03:26.840 --> 00:03:29.720
This is a biological system overload.

64
00:03:29.720 --> 00:03:34.520
At this stage, traditional verbal
interventions usually escalate the distress.

65
00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:39.720
Spark utilizes a specific protocol for
these moments, safety, silence,

66
00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:44.040
and space. While many traditional tech
interfaces or parenting styles

67
00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:48.160
attempt to reestabl-ish control or
discipline during a crisis, SPARC

68
00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:52.880
remains hands-off. It provides regulatory
support by simply being present

69
00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:58.000
and quiet. This methodology treats
neurodivergence as a functional operating

70
00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:00.880
system to be respected, rather than a
condition to be

71
00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:02.480
managed through force.

72
00:04:02.480 --> 00:04:06.320
By removing the language of demands, SPARC
offers a blueprint

73
00:04:06.320 --> 00:04:08.960
for how we might build technology in the
future.

74
00:04:08.960 --> 00:04:11.760
It demonstrates that AI can move away from
the role

75
00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:16.160
of a task-oriented servant to become a
non-coercive companion that

76
00:04:16.160 --> 00:04:19.520
prioritizes human safety and
understanding.

